---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Papers from '../components/Papers.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: 'Research & Publications — Cody Peterson',
  url: 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/research/',
  author: { '@id': 'https://www.cody-peterson.com/#person' },
};
---
<Base title="Research & Publications" description="Homeric philology, archetypal psychology, and the design of AI-assisted research programmes. Publications, questions, and tools by Cody Peterson." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="page-header research-header">
    <div class="page-header-inner">
      <div class="folio"><span>Research &amp; publications</span><em>Texts · Feeling · Value</em></div>
      <h1>Homer and the<br /><em>history of feeling.</em></h1>
      <p class="subtitle">What inherited language preserves of feeling and the formation of value—and how we can return to the evidence.</p>
      <nav class="page-jumps" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#questions">Questions</a><a href="#method">Method</a><a href="#publications">Publications</a><a href="#tools">Tools &amp; programmes</a></nav>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section paper-section" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
    <div class="section-inner research-intro">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">The inquiry</span><h2 id="questions-title">What does language<br /><em>preserve of feeling?</em></h2></div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>My research works at the border of Homeric philology and archetypal psychology. I am interested in the soul as it appears in inherited language: in the organs that feel, the words that name endurance, and the forms through which experience acquires value.</p>
        <p>This inquiry grew out of writing about recovery. <em>The Shadow of a Figure of Light</em> follows the relation between Jung and the Twelve Steps. My Homeric work returns to an older vocabulary of feeling and asks what it can contribute to depth psychology now.</p>
        <p>The questions extend beyond individual images and archetypes to grammar, translation, and the ways later readers use ancient texts. A translation is already an interpretation. Returning to the language allows us to examine what that interpretation makes visible.</p>
        <div class="passage-example"><p class="work-status">A passage to begin with · Odyssey 20.17–23</p><h3>Odysseus speaks to his heart.</h3><p>He recalls the heart’s earlier endurance; the scene then describes it obeying and remaining in endurance. That gives the inquiry something precise to follow: the relation between the person who speaks and the heart he addresses.</p><p>When a later translation or philosophical reading retells this scene, who is made to act, obey, or bear what remains? The textual comparison comes first. What it means for a psychology of the soul is the question I bring to it.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="research-intro">
        <div><span class="eyebrow">Research programme design</span><h2 id="method-title">Beyond the <em>specialist fortress.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Jung urged psychologists to leave the “thickly walled specialist fortress” of their own discipline. I design AI-assisted research programmes that put that invitation into practice across texts and traditions.</p><p class="source-note">Jung, “Psychology and Literature,” introduction, <em>Collected Works</em> 15.</p>
          <p>AI helps with source discovery, research organization, software development, and testing proposed readings. Generated output is provisional working material, never a source. I take responsibility for the judgments, arguments, and final wording.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="method-sequence">
        <li><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Return to the passage</h3><p>Keep the original wording, edition, translation, and citation available beside the interpretation.</p></li>
        <li><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Ask of the corpus</h3><p>Define what has been searched and how forms have been classified. Examine the exceptions as closely as the pattern.</p></li>
        <li><span class="method-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Make the reading answerable</h3><p>Check machine-assisted results against sources. Preserve counterexamples and distinguish an observed distribution from the psychological argument drawn from it.</p></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="research-method-detail"><div><span class="eyebrow">What a result can establish</span><h3>Evidence and interpretation.</h3></div><div class="prose"><p>My Homeric work joins close reading to reproducible corpus analysis. A count or grammatical pattern establishes something about the texts examined. The psychological interpretation is a further argument: a reader can accept the distribution and disagree with what I make of it.</p><p>Named editions, passage references, stated comparison rules, and the limits of each study belong with the argument. The aim is to make the work answerable to other readers, including those who arrive at a different conclusion.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="publications" aria-labelledby="publications-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <header class="section-header"><span class="eyebrow">Publication record</span><h2 id="publications-title">Writing <em>in print and in press.</em></h2></header>
      <div class="research-publications">
        <article class="publication publication-book">
          <a href="/book/" class="publication-book-image"><img src="/images/book-cover.jpg" alt="The Shadow of a Figure of Light, book cover" width="400" height="600" loading="lazy" /></a>
          <div><p class="work-status">Published · 2024</p><h3><a href="/book/">The Shadow of a Figure of Light</a></h3><p class="publication-citation"><em>The Archetype of the Alcoholic and the Journey to Enlightenment.</em> Chiron Publications.</p><p>Jung, Bill Wilson, and the Twelve Steps as a modern myth of transformation.</p><a class="text-link" href="/book/">About the book <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
        </article>
        <Papers />
      </div>
      <div class="research-profile-links"><a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2028-0154">ORCID <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=a8xhFSgAAAAJ">Google Scholar <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Cody-Peterson-6/research">ResearchGate <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="tools" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <header class="section-header"><span class="eyebrow">Tools &amp; programmes</span><h2 id="tools-title">Building a way <em>into the sources.</em></h2><p>Research tools grow alongside the writing, each with its own object of attention.</p></header>
      <div class="instrument-list">
        <article class="instrument"><div class="instrument-name"><span class="work-status">Depth psychology</span><h3><a href="https://www.seba.health/">Seba.Health <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3></div><p>I founded Seba to help people find the literature, vocabulary, and practitioners of depth psychology. It brings together research resources, study tools, and a practitioner directory, operated on a not-for-profit basis.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.seba.health/">Explore Seba <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
        <article class="instrument"><div class="instrument-name"><span class="work-status">Philological workbench</span><h3><a href="https://logoi.health/">Logoi <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3></div><p>Read a text, search a corpus, study a word, compare versions, and analyze usage. The workbench keeps the edition and passage attached to the result so a reader can return to the evidence.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://logoi.health/">Open Logoi <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
        <article class="instrument"><div class="instrument-name"><span class="work-status">In development</span><h3>The stories are next</h3></div><p>A further programme takes up the world’s myths and narrative traditions. It extends the inquiry from the vocabulary of the soul to the stories through which people have imagined it.</p><span class="instrument-note">Ongoing research</span></article>
      </div>
      <div class="research-method-detail"><div><span class="eyebrow">Seba, Sebastian &amp; my scholarship</span><h3>Distinct kinds of work.</h3></div><div class="prose"><p>The directory helps people find practitioners. The library and research tools help readers explore a tradition. Sebastian offers AI-assisted conversations about texts, dreams, and images; these are exploratory conversations, not clinical care.</p><p>Listed practitioners and contributors speak for themselves. The arguments published under my name are my own; a directory listing does not imply endorsement of those arguments or of Sebastian.</p></div></div>
      <div class="research-contact prose"><h3>In conversation</h3><p>For seminars, lectures, research collaboration, or a conversation about these questions, write to <a href="mailto:cody@seba.health">cody@seba.health</a>. Recorded talks are collected in <a href="/videos/">Lectures</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
